INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Living Jedi Testament I: Awareness','jedi-testament-awareness','Awareness begins with distinguishing what happens from the story we tell about it. An emotion is an experience, not necessarily an accurate explanation of another person''s intentions. A Jedi can acknowledge anger without treating anger as a command.

Practice three distinctions: observation versus inference, feeling versus action, and uncertainty versus ignorance. Before responding to a disagreement, describe the observable facts and identify what remains unknown. This creates room for judgment without requiring emotional suppression.

Theological reflection: whether the Force is understood as sacred presence or interdependence, awareness invites attention to relationships beyond immediate desires. It does not make intuition infallible.

Study assignment: record a misunderstanding, identify the assumption that shaped it, and describe what evidence would change your interpretation.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Living Jedi Testament II: Knowledge','jedi-testament-knowledge','Knowledge is a responsibility rather than a badge of superiority. A guardian must distinguish testimony, inference, evidence and conviction. Spiritual belief can be meaningful while remaining distinct from empirical claims.

Intellectual humility does not mean accepting every assertion equally. Evaluate sources, examine competing explanations and acknowledge uncertainty. A teacher who cannot tolerate questions undermines the very discipline of learning.

Practice: choose a disputed claim and identify its strongest supporting evidence and strongest objection. Explain the opposing position in terms its advocate would recognize.

Assessment: describe a belief you revised and the reasons for doing so. Growth is demonstrated by honest correction, not by pretending never to have been mistaken.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Living Jedi Testament III: Compassion','jedi-testament-compassion','Compassion recognizes suffering and dignity without requiring agreement, intimacy or unlimited access. It differs from possessiveness because it does not treat another person''s choices as property. It differs from indulgence because care may require boundaries and accountability.

A guardian must consider both immediate relief and long-term consequences. Helping without listening can impose unwanted solutions. Forgiveness, reconciliation and trust are separate decisions; none is automatically owed.

Practice: ask what assistance is wanted before acting. When assistance is declined, respect that decision unless an immediate safety emergency requires appropriate intervention.

Discussion: how can a guardian remain compassionate toward an adversary while protecting those affected by harmful conduct?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='jedi-temple' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'The Sovereign Flame I: Passion','sith-flame-passion','Passion reveals what carries significance, but intensity alone does not establish truth or worth. Desire can originate in chosen values, social pressure, fear or habit. The sovereign examines these origins rather than worshipping every impulse.

Distinguish aspiration from compulsion: an aspiration permits reflection and revision, while a compulsion can narrow perceived alternatives. Choosing a goal deliberately gives passion direction.

Practice: name three ambitions and identify their personal meaning, costs and realistic next steps. Consider whether each would still matter without an audience or rival.

Theological reflection: a Sith-inspired practitioner may regard passion as sacred creative energy or a metaphor for motivation. Neither interpretation requires surrendering judgment.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'The Sovereign Flame II: Strength','sith-flame-strength','Strength is the capacity to meet difficulty with skill, adaptability and judgment. It includes physical capability, emotional literacy, knowledge, patience and the willingness to ask for help. Dependence on intimidation is not proof of independence.

Discipline transforms intention into repeatable action. Sustainable practice includes rest, feedback and revision. Injury, exhaustion and humiliation are not necessary rites of advancement.

Practice: select one skill, establish a realistic baseline, schedule manageable practice and review progress weekly. Compare performance against your own previous work rather than another person''s worth.

Discussion: when does refusing assistance demonstrate autonomy, and when does it merely preserve pride at the expense of competence?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'The Sovereign Flame III: Power','sith-flame-power','Power can mean the capacity to act, access resources, create, negotiate or influence institutions. It can also mean control over others. These meanings must not be confused. A person who depends on another''s fear may possess influence while remaining captive to that relationship.

Self-sovereignty requires informed choice, meaningful alternatives and responsibility. Consent and transparent agreements allow people to cooperate without surrendering their agency.

Practice: map a constructive goal, the resources it requires, the obstacles involved and the people affected. Identify ways to increase your capabilities without coercion or deception.

Discussion: what distinguishes legitimate leadership from domination, and what safeguards allow followers to disagree or leave?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='order-of-the-sith' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';